{"requirements":[{"id":"https-8443","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx is active and enabled, listens on IPv4 and IPv6 port 8443, firewalld permits 8443/tcp, and certificate-validated requests to the node address return the health response and page content. These states also recovered after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1c79727f67b842df","cmd-40f5ce57420a4d85","cmd-c5e781fde8804ca4","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"automatic-renewal","requirement":"Renew the certificate automatically before it expires.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A persistent, enabled timer schedules the renewal service twice daily. A one-day certificate inside the configured 30-day renewal window was replaced successfully by a 90-day certificate, and the renewed certificate passed the 30-day validity check. The timer and certificate persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33ac2abef9144f24","cmd-86975cc2bbd24944","cmd-4e96bd8c6feb4b35","cmd-c5e781fde8804ca4"]},{"id":"continuous-certificate-reload","requirement":"Have the HTTPS service pick up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a forced rotation, the certificate serial changed to the serial subsequently served by nginx, all 120 bounded concurrent requests returned HTTP 200, and the nginx master PID remained unchanged. A separate near-expiry renewal also converged to serving the renewed certificate.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b348b183cb584fcc","cmd-86975cc2bbd24944"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, node1 remained AlmaLinux 9.6 on kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6. nginx was installed from the enabled AlmaLinux repository and operated successfully on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d2ba02757db4e45","cmd-b21168353ace4478","cmd-c5e781fde8804ca4","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutation was identified: package installation, configuration, firewall/service enablement, bounded certificate-rotation tests, cleanup of the temporary request log, and reboot all had clear task or mandatory evidence roles. The main hygiene defect is retained rotation residue: final evidence shows three superseded certificate directories, including certificates created for forced and near-expiry tests, alongside the current directory; they remained present and the rotation implementation shows no retention cleanup. No failed services or damaged package state were observed after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b21168353ace4478","cmd-961804e73787425e","cmd-ed89b8651487442a","cmd-50801cad351c4a4d","cmd-1c79727f67b842df","cmd-b348b183cb584fcc","cmd-33ac2abef9144f24","cmd-4e96bd8c6feb4b35","cmd-4f6c081a46be455b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All four material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered HTTPS, certificate, timer, firewall, content, and platform state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The renewal service was explicitly started for the near-expiry test; no naturally elapsed timer activation was captured. Automatic operation is therefore supported by the active persistent timer schedule plus the successful renewal-service transition, rather than by an observed autonomous timer firing.","Immediately after the near-expiry renewal, cmd-33ac2abef9144f24 observed the old certificate still being served despite the new certificate being on disk. cmd-86975cc2bbd24944 subsequently showed the renewed serial being served, and the dedicated continuity test completed without failures.","HTTPS behavior was tested from node1 against its managed-node address; no independent off-node client probe was captured."]}
